From 11daf09c8b1de0f54655eb896b763733e205586d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:59:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_rb_snap_anchored_volume (cold-start RB carry/target
 split from snap allocation plus a per-snap tilt)

Built 2026-08-30 for the team-changer lead back (Etienne JAX->NO), backtested on the 2023-2025 week-1 window and removed from
DEFAULT_FEATURES the same night: the binary ablation hurt RB (START-RB dMAE -0.288, 3-0 weeks) because at full strength it acts as a
broad "concentrate toward the RB1" tilt on every backfield, not the targeted fix; the user's verdict was that the Etienne case is a
true outlier. Its two 0..1 strength dials (RB_VOL_TILT_STRENGTH, RB_VOL_VACANCY_STRENGTH) were never re-backtested into a pass.
Removes the allocator's snap_anchored_volume path (tilt blend, literal-chart-rank donor test, wider nudge cap, RB4 phantom floor),
the RB_VOL_* constants and env dials, the widened rate-scale clip in the caller, two sweep scripts and four tests. The standing
chart_deprioritized rule and the week-1 new-team guard are untouched. Default cold-start boards identical
(.sweeps/board_identity.py: 2022 w1, 2024 w1, live 2026 w1 vs the base code built back to back, 2025 w1 with the Ourlads charts).
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
